title The journey that opens on measurement -- LOCA seated, and a reading on Mind's direction
prompt Keaton asked for an expanded prompt carrying a journey seat with my plan, and whether to keep running Mind or let Sound take over until Mind's direction is fixed.
think A ladder cannot open without a waymark drawn, so LOCA came first: derived from macos-native-surface-rye-backend at index 2761, seated in the sealed registry with the body resealed and its witness GREEN on metal, in the rule table, and in the derive tool's own input constant.
think Five quests rather than an open-ended plan, because a journey is five quests under the panchanga and because each of these genuinely closes: the view that owns its drawing, input into the event ring contract, the application shell, one surface over two backends, and the iOS door. Each names what it proves, what it refuses to claim, and the one thing that stops it and asks.
think Every rung is marked by waymark, name, and stamp rather than an ascending number -- the mark law closed one week ago and the meter enforcing it landed three hours ago, so this is the first ladder seated under both.
obs On Mind: its work is good and its aim is unresolved, which are different problems with different answers. Three proven candidates today, every one a refusal proof that the Rye port will have to pass -- so the Swift is the specification even where it is not the shipping code. Running it harder into a lane being re-aimed spends laps twice; stopping it loses a proof-writer.
obs The reading I carried to Keaton: pause the loop rather than the star, restart it on a re-aimed seat, and let Sound take the macOS surface meanwhile -- which is this seat's own lane by the six-bodies charter anyway, and needs no supervisor update to begin.
